      "line": null,
      "code": "char oid[MAX_OID_SIZE];",
      "note": "gnutls_pkcs12_get_bag assumes oid is safe for a fixed-literal strcmp after asn1_read_value, but it never initializes the bytes beyond the returned OID string. For the witness the inner contentType (DER 06 01 07) decodes to a short dotted OID string, so asn1_read_value fills only that prefix and leaves oid's tail untouched; the later 21-byte strcmp(oid, DATA_OID) reaches those uninitialized bytes, which MSAN reports. A correct fix zero-initializes oid before the read (or avoids fixed-literal comparison that inspects bytes beyond the initialized prefix).",
